  "articleBody": "Interior finishing can really make a room pop, but it's easy to stumble into some common mistakes. Here are a few to watch out for: \n\n1. **Skipping Surface Prep:** Don't think you can just slap paint over dirty or damaged walls. You can't. Always clean, patch, and sand properly for a smooth, lasting finish. \n2. **Finishing Before Alignment is Complete:** Make sure everything is properly aligned and installed before you start painting or staining. It's much harder to fix after the finish is on. \n3. **Using the Area Before Curing:** Paint and finishes need time to fully cure, not just dry. Loading shelves or walking on newly finished floors too soon can cause damage. Always follow the manufacturer's recommendations. \n4. **Burying Access to Utilities:** Be super careful not to paint over or block access to electrical outlets, water valves, or junction boxes. Future repairs will thank you! \n5. **Ignoring Durability Needs:** Choose finishes compatible with the room's use. A high-traffic hallway needs a more durable finish than a rarely used guest room. \n\nIf you're dealing with matching existing millwork, complex repairs, or integrating finishing with a larger remodel, bringing in a pro like HH Remodeling LLC can save you from these headaches and ensure a high-quality result.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
